        q: "You are a PM at a fintech that has just received a show cause notice from SEBI for a feature in your investment product that SEBI considers to be investment advice without a registered investment advisor license. Legal says this could result in a significant fine. How do you handle the next 48 hours?",
        a: `The first thing I do in the next 48 hours is make sure I am not the decision maker. This is a legal and regulatory matter and my role is to support the response, not lead it.\n\nBut as the PM who owns the feature, I have specific responsibilities that nobody else can fulfill as quickly.\n\nIn the first two hours I pull together a complete product documentation package for the legal team. Every version of the feature that has been live, every copy string, every algorithm or rule that drives the output, every user flow diagram, and the original PRD with the regulatory risk section. If the legal team is going to respond to SEBI accurately, they need to understand exactly what the feature does and what it was designed to do.\n\nI also pull the usage data. How many users have accessed this feature? What actions did they take after seeing the output? Did they invest based on it? This data shapes the severity assessment and influences the legal strategy.\n\nIn parallel I work with engineering to understand the fastest path to modify or disable the feature if that becomes the legal recommendation. I do not disable it unilaterally before legal advises me to because taking down a live feature can sometimes be interpreted as an admission of guilt in a regulatory context. But I want to know that if legal says disable it in the next 12 hours, I can execute that in under two hours.\n\nThe 48 hour goal is to give our legal team everything they need to draft an accurate response to SEBI and to give leadership a clear picture of our options. The options are typically modify the feature to remove the elements SEBI has flagged, disable the feature while we obtain the appropriate registration, or defend the original design with legal argument.\n\nWhat I do not do in the next 48 hours is communicate anything externally about this matter until legal has cleared the communication. In a SEBI matter, premature external communication creates additional problems.`,
